# class: adr
# schema: id | title | status | summary | source
# source-glob: docs/adr/*.md
# recipe: builtin:adr

ADR-0001 | Per-service topology derivation — five-pass algorithm on the read side | accepted | Topology derived read-side per request via five-pass algorithm (bucket-by-env, explicit-first, correlation-fallback, merge, dangling); no stored topology rows | @docs/adr/ADR-0001-topology-derivation-five-pass.md
ADR-0002 | Modular monolith — single API container hosting two library surfaces | superseded by ADR-0006 (2026-05-19) | Co-location mechanics retained as historical record: one ASP.NET host (backend/api/) composes write-api/ + read-api/ libraries + shared/; single Dockerfile; X-Api-Key on Write group only; future split is host+gateway-config change. Framing reset by ADR-0006 (microservices architecture; co-location is a packaging choice) | @docs/adr/ADR-0002-modular-monolith-consolidation.md
ADR-0003 | Theme persistence in localStorage with FOIT-safe inline bootstrap | accepted | Theme preference in localStorage.dashboard.theme; FOIT-safe inline-script bootstrap before SPA boot sets <html data-theme>; single writer post-bootstrap (ThemeService in frontend/shared/) | @docs/adr/ADR-0003-theme-persistence-and-foit-safe-bootstrap.md
ADR-0004 | Opaque per-progress_reporter cursor; backend-held; out-of-process fetcher; plug-in adapter shape | accepted (paired with CR-0009) | 4 decisions: (1) cursor lives on backend not fetcher container via GET/PUT /api/fetcher/state/{source-id}; (2) cursor is opaque per-progress_reporter blob VARCHAR(4096) keyed by (progress_reporter, source_id) - backend never parses; (3) fetcher runs in separate container (Dashboard.Fetcher.Host) not in-process BackgroundService (NFR-05 preservation + opt-in + failure isolation + credential isolation; minReplicas=maxReplicas=1 when enabled); (4) ICiCdAdapter plug-in shape with AdapterId + FetchPageAsync(sourceId, opaqueCursor, pageSize, ct) -> (events, newCursor, hasMore); host owns scheduler/retry/back-off/Write-API dispatch | @docs/adr/ADR-0004-opaque-per-progress-reporter-cursor.md
ADR-0005 | Release-install migration actuation via tag-pinned migration.sql release asset | accepted | Release installer pulls tag-pinned migration.sql GitHub Release asset and applies via one-shot postgres:16-alpine container (profile-gated, default-on); idempotent contract; no source tree / SDK on install host; local-dev SDK+bind-mount flow unchanged | @docs/adr/ADR-0005-release-install-migration-actuation.md
ADR-0006 | Microservices architecture with container co-location of Write + Read API services | accepted (2026-05-19) — supersedes ADR-0002 | Reframes the backend architecture: project is microservices (Write API, Read API, Fetcher, Frontend SPA, Gateway — distinct services with distinct concerns); Write + Read API services co-located in dashboard-api image for operational simplicity within NFR-02; co-location is a packaging choice, not the architecture itself. Zero code/infra/Dockerfile change; ADR-0002 co-location mechanics + future-split trigger conditions survive as historical record. Frontend "modular monolith" Angular-workspace wording is a different concept (Angular libraries pattern) and stays | @docs/adr/ADR-0006-microservices-architecture-with-container-co-location.md
